.TH AD_RECORD 1 "2026-08-21" "ad 2.0" "ad scripts"
.SH NAME
ad_record \- record animation to a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ad_record
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
NAME\fR
    ad_record.sh — Record an animation's timed op stream for later replay\fR
\fR
SYNOPSIS\fR
    ad_record.sh [-h|--help]\fR
    ad_record.sh <oldfile> <newfile> <recording.dv>\fR
\fR
DESCRIPTION\fR
    Runs the ad_vim compute + postprocess + pace pipeline on an\fR
    old/new file pair and writes the resulting TIMED op stream (with\fR
    delay, keep, delete, insert ops) to a recording file. The\fR
    recording can then be replayed by dv_replay.sh without needing\fR
    the original new file — only the old file (initial buffer) is\fR
    needed at replay time.\fR
\fR
    Intermediate files are written to /tmp/dv_raw.txt and\fR
    /tmp/dv_post.txt (overwritten each run).\fR
\fR
OPTIONS\fR
    -h, --help       Show this help message and exit 0.\fR
    <oldfile>        Path to the original/source file (initial buffer).\fR
    <newfile>         Path to the target file the animation should reach.\fR
    <recording.dv>    Path where the timed op stream will be saved.\fR
\fR
EXAMPLES\fR
    ad_record.sh tests/tests/examples/01_small_python/old.py \\fR
                tests/tests/examples/01_small_python/new.py \\fR
                /tmp/my_recording.dv\fR
        Record the animation that transforms old.py into new.py,\fR
        saving the timed op stream to /tmp/my_recording.dv.\fR
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show detailed help and exit
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ad_vim (1)
